From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yah <yah@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:50:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 54/75] 0060-loom-concat-reserves-explicit-registers-early

Loom: a concat whose result lives in explicit physical registers (AIE2P) is reserved from its earliest unit's start
with per-unit start points, as fragmented tied-source assemblies already are: a whole register cannot be split, so a
piece placed before the reservation forces copies of the others. GPU sets byte-identical; changes 15 of the NPU
split's 27 images (NPU gate: pp2048 split window 00 bit-identical,
hidden / logits / all_logits md5 equal).

(cherry picked from commit 14fa9268710c0bc1dcf63747df6e6992f8e2f951)
---
 loom/src/loom/codegen/low/allocation/concat_reservation.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/loom/src/loom/codegen/low/allocation/concat_reservation.c b/loom/src/loom/codegen/low/allocation/concat_reservation.c
index ab9dd15ff2..c2d25ee577 100644
--- a/loom/src/loom/codegen/low/allocation/concat_reservation.c
+++ b/loom/src/loom/codegen/low/allocation/concat_reservation.c
@@ -888,7 +888,13 @@ iree_status_t loom_low_allocation_concat_reservation_find(
       loom_low_allocation_unit_liveness_start_points_for_value_ordinal(
           context->unit_liveness, context->liveness, relation->result_ordinal);
   IREE_ASSERT(result_unit_start_points != NULL);
+  // Explicit physical register results are reserved from their first unit's
+  // start with per-unit start points: a whole register cannot be split, so a
+  // piece placed before the reservation would force a copy of the others.
   const bool has_fragmented_tied_source_assembly =
+      loom_low_reg_class_uses_explicit_physical_registers(
+          &context->descriptor_set
+               ->reg_classes[capacity.descriptor_reg_class_id]) ||
       loom_low_allocation_concat_reservation_has_fragmented_tied_source_assembly(
           context, result_range, result_unit_start_points);
   // Scalar sources can cheaply reserve a future aggregate, and packet-local
